IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-solvency`
IMPORT `sga2-nouns`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: s 76(9A), (9B), (9BA), (9C), (9CA) and (9D) -- the three routes by which a company may give financial
-- assistance on a resolution of its board (the 10 percent route, the unanimous-members route and the route that does not materially prejudice), the two bars that
-- end them, and the saving for directors' duties.
-- Layer 1. Each condition of each route is its own function; a route function takes the answers of its conditions as facts and answers JUST TRUE when every one holds.
--
-- HOW THE ROUTES ANSWER. "Nothing in subsection (1) prohibits the giving by a company of financial assistance ... if (a) ... (g)": a carve-out, named for a permission.
--   JUST TRUE  every condition is met;
--   NOTHING    a condition is not met: the paragraph then says nothing, and subsection (1) decides by its own words (the grant rule of 2026-11-12, limit 1; marker {F-A7}).
-- Each condition function answers JUST TRUE when it is met and JUST FALSE when it is not (the condition is the limb's own question).
-- Periods are counted by sg-periods.l4 (P1 to P9 of the keel). Public holidays are a list the caller supplies (s 4(1) "business day").
-- The solvency statement is the core's `Solvency statement`; whether it is one is the keel's `s 7A(1) the statement is a solvency statement`.

§ `Section 76(9A): the route within 10 percent of paid-up capital and reserves`

-- (9A)(a): the amount of the assistance, together with any other assistance given under this subsection whose repayment remains outstanding, would not exceed 10% of the aggregate
-- of (i) the total paid-up capital and (ii) the reserves of the company, as disclosed in the most recent financial statements of the company that comply with section 201.
-- src:7590 | (9A) Nothing in subsection (1) prohibits the giving by a company
-- src:7591 | of financial assistance for the purpose of, or in connection with, an
-- src:7592 | acquisition or proposed acquisition by a person of shares or units of
-- src:7593 | shares in the company or in a holding company or ultimate holding
-- src:7594 | company (as the case may be) of the company if —
-- src:7596 | (a) the amount of the financial assistance, together with any
-- src:7597 | other financial assistance given by the company under this
-- src:7598 | subsection repayment of which remains outstanding,
-- src:7599 | would not exceed 10% of the aggregate of —
-- src:7601 | (i) the total paid‑up capital of the company; and
-- src:7603 | (ii) the reserves of the company,
-- src:7605 | (a) as disclosed in the most recent financial statements of the
-- src:7606 | company that comply with section 201;
@ref s 76(9A)(a) (src:7590-7606)
GIVEN `the amount of the financial assistance, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of other financial assistance given by the company under subsection (9A) and still outstanding, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the total paid-up capital of the company, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the reserves of the company, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `those figures are disclosed in the most recent financial statements of the company that comply with section 201` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(9A)(a) the assistance is within 10 percent of paid-up capital and reserves` MEANS
    IF    `those figures are disclosed in the most recent financial statements of the company that comply with section 201`
      AND (`the amount of the financial assistance, in Singapore dollars` PLUS `the amount of other financial assistance given by the company under subsection (9A) and still outstanding, in Singapore dollars`)
          AT MOST (10% TIMES (`the total paid-up capital of the company, in Singapore dollars` PLUS `the reserves of the company, in Singapore dollars`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if (a) the amount of the financial assistance, together with any other financial assistance given by the company under this subsection repayment of which remains outstanding, would not exceed 10% of the aggregate of (i) the total paid-up capital of the company; and (ii) the reserves of the company, as disclosed in the most recent financial statements" -- a condition introduced by "if", unmet

-- (9A)(b): the company receives fair value in connection with the financial assistance.
-- src:7608 | (b) the company receives fair value in connection with the
-- src:7609 | financial assistance;
@ref s 76(9A)(b) (src:7608-7609)
GIVEN `the company receives fair value in connection with the financial assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(9A)(b) the company receives fair value` MEANS
    IF `the company receives fair value in connection with the financial assistance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if ... (b) the company receives fair value in connection with the financial assistance" -- a condition introduced by "if", unmet

-- (9A)(c): the board of directors of the company passes a resolution that (i) the company should give the assistance; (ii) giving the assistance is in the best interests of the
-- company; and (iii) the terms and conditions under which the assistance is given are fair and reasonable to the company.
-- src:7611 | (c) the board of directors of the company passes a resolution
-- src:7612 | that —
-- src:7614 | (i) the company should give the assistance;
-- src:7616 | (ii) giving the assistance is in the best interests of the
-- src:7617 | company; and
-- src:7619 | (iii) the terms and conditions under which the assistance
-- src:7620 | is given are fair and reasonable to the company;
@ref s 76(9A)(c) (src:7611-7620)
GIVEN `the board of directors of the company has passed a resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution says the company should give the assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution says giving the assistance is in the best interests of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution says the terms and conditions under which the assistance is given are fair and reasonable to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(9A)(c) the board has passed the resolution the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF    `the board of directors of the company has passed a resolution`
      AND `the resolution says the company should give the assistance`
      AND `the resolution says giving the assistance is in the best interests of the company`
      AND `the resolution says the terms and conditions under which the assistance is given are fair and reasonable to the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if ... (c) the board of directors of the company passes a resolution that (i) the company should give the assistance; (ii) giving the assistance is in the best interests of the company; and (iii) the terms and conditions ... are fair and reasonable to the company" -- a condition introduced by "if", unmet

-- (9A)(d): the resolution sets out in full the grounds for the directors' conclusions.
-- src:7622 | (d) the resolution sets out in full the grounds for the directors’
-- src:7623 | conclusions;
@ref s 76(9A)(d) (src:7622-7623)
GIVEN `the resolution sets out in full the grounds for the directors' conclusions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(9A)(d) the resolution sets out the grounds` MEANS
    IF `the resolution sets out in full the grounds for the directors' conclusions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if ... (d) the resolution sets out in full the grounds for the directors' conclusions" -- a condition introduced by "if", unmet

-- (9A)(e): all the directors of the company make a solvency statement in relation to the giving of the financial assistance.
-- Whether the statement is a solvency statement is s 7A(1) (keel); "all the directors make" is a fact (fork F-A9: "make" against "sign").
-- src:7625 | (e) all the directors of the company make a solvency statement
-- src:7626 | in relation to the giving of the financial assistance;
@ref s 76(9A)(e) (src:7625-7626)
GIVEN statement IS A `Solvency statement`
      `the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the directors of the company have made the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(9A)(e) all the directors have made a solvency statement` MEANS
    IF    statement's `the proposal it concerns` EQUALS `a giving of financial assistance under section 76(9A) or (9B)`
      AND `all the directors of the company have made the statement`
      AND (`s 7A(1) the statement is a solvency statement` statement `the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if ... (e) all the directors of the company make a solvency statement in relation to the giving of the financial assistance" -- a condition introduced by "if", unmet

-- (9A)(f): within 10 business days of providing the assistance, the company sends to each member a notice containing particulars of (i) the class and number of shares or units
-- of shares in respect of which the assistance was or is to be given; (ii) the consideration paid or payable for them; (iii) the identity of the person receiving the assistance and, if that
-- person is not the beneficial owner, of the beneficial owner; and (iv) the nature and, if quantifiable, the amount of the assistance.
-- src:7628 | (f) within 10 business days of providing the financial
-- src:7629 | assistance, the company sends to each member a notice
-- src:7630 | containing particulars of —
-- src:7632 | (i) the class and number of shares or units of shares in
-- src:7633 | respect of which the financial assistance was or is to
-- src:7634 | be given;
-- src:7639 | (ii) the consideration paid or payable for those shares or
-- src:7640 | units of shares;
-- src:7642 | (iii) the identity of the person receiving the financial
-- src:7643 | assistance and, if that person is not the beneficial
-- src:7644 | owner of those shares or units of shares, the identity
-- src:7645 | of the beneficial owner; and
-- src:7647 | (iv) the nature and, if quantifiable, the amount of the
-- src:7648 | financial assistance; and
@ref s 76(9A)(f) (src:7628-7648)
GIVEN `the day the financial assistance was provided` IS A DATE
      `the day the notice was sent to each member` IS A DATE
      `the company has sent each member a notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice gives the class and number of shares or units of shares in respect of which the financial assistance was or is to be given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice gives the consideration paid or payable for those shares or units of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice gives the identity of the person receiving the financial assistance and, if that person is not the beneficial owner, the identity of the beneficial owner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice gives the nature and, if quantifiable, the amount of the financial assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(9A)(f) the company has sent each member the notice in time` MEANS
    IF    `the company has sent each member a notice`
      AND `the notice gives the class and number of shares or units of shares in respect of which the financial assistance was or is to be given`
      AND `the notice gives the consideration paid or payable for those shares or units of shares`
      AND `the notice gives the identity of the person receiving the financial assistance and, if that person is not the beneficial owner, the identity of the beneficial owner`
      AND `the notice gives the nature and, if quantifiable, the amount of the financial assistance`
      AND `the day the notice was sent to each member` AT MOST `period: the last day of a number of business days after` `the day the financial assistance was provided` 10 `the public holidays`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if ... (f) within 10 business days of providing the financial assistance, the company sends to each member a notice containing particulars of" -- a condition introduced by "if", unmet; a period the text fixes (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a)); an early notice is not excluded (fork F-A8)

-- (9A)(g): not later than the business day next following the day when the notice mentioned in (f) is sent to members, the company lodges with the Registrar a copy of that
-- notice and a copy of the solvency statement mentioned in (e).
-- src:7650 | (g) not later than the business day next following the day when
-- src:7651 | the notice mentioned in paragraph (f) is sent to members of
-- src:7652 | the company, the company lodges with the Registrar a
-- src:7653 | copy of that notice and a copy of the solvency statement
-- src:7654 | mentioned in paragraph (e).
@ref s 76(9A)(g) (src:7650-7654)
GIVEN `the day the notice was sent to each member` IS A DATE
      `the day the company lodged the copies with the Registrar` IS A DATE
      `the company lodged a copy of the notice with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company lodged a copy of the solvency statement with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(9A)(g) the company has lodged the copies with the Registrar in time` MEANS
    IF    `the company lodged a copy of the notice with the Registrar`
      AND `the company lodged a copy of the solvency statement with the Registrar`
      AND `the day the company lodged the copies with the Registrar` AT MOST `period: the last day of a number of business days after` `the day the notice was sent to each member` 1 `the public holidays`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if ... (g) not later than the business day next following the day when the notice mentioned in paragraph (f) is sent to members of the company, the company lodges with the Registrar a copy of that notice and a copy of the solvency statement" -- a condition introduced by "if", unmet; a period the text fixes (item (a)); early lodging is not excluded (fork F-A8)

-- (9A) as a whole: nothing in subsection (1) prohibits the giving of financial assistance if (a) to (g).
-- src:7590 | (9A) Nothing in subsection (1) prohibits the giving by a company
-- src:7591 | of financial assistance for the purpose of, or in connection with, an
-- src:7592 | acquisition or proposed acquisition by a person of shares or units of
-- src:7593 | shares in the company or in a holding company or ultimate holding
-- src:7594 | company (as the case may be) of the company if —
@ref s 76(9A) (src:7590-7594)
GIVEN `the condition in paragraph (a) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition in paragraph (b) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition in paragraph (c) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition in paragraph (d) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition in paragraph (e) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition in paragraph (f) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition in paragraph (g) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(9A) subsection (1) does not prohibit the giving of the assistance` MEANS
    IF    `the condition in paragraph (a) is met`
      AND `the condition in paragraph (b) is met`
      AND `the condition in paragraph (c) is met`
      AND `the condition in paragraph (d) is met`
      AND `the condition in paragraph (e) is met`
      AND `the condition in paragraph (f) is met`
      AND `the condition in paragraph (g) is met`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Nothing in subsection (1) prohibits the giving by a company of financial assistance ... if (a) ... (g)" -- a carve-out named for a permission whose "if" gate failed: the subsection says nothing, and subsection (1) decides {F-A7}

