    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the members passed the resolution` `the day the financial assistance is given` 12 Months
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if ... (g) the financial assistance is given not more than 12 months after the resolution mentioned in paragraph (e) is passed" -- a condition introduced by "if", unmet; a period the text fixes (item (a)); assistance before the resolution is not excluded by these words (fork F-A8)

-- (9B) as a whole: nothing in subsection (1) prohibits the giving of financial assistance if (a) to (g).
