      `the condition in paragraph (c) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition in paragraph (d) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition in paragraph (e) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition in paragraph (f) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition in paragraph (g) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(9B) subsection (1) does not prohibit the giving of the assistance` MEANS
    IF    `the condition in paragraph (a) is met`
      AND `the condition in paragraph (b) is met`
      AND `the condition in paragraph (c) is met`
      AND `the condition in paragraph (d) is met`
      AND `the condition in paragraph (e) is met`
      AND `the condition in paragraph (f) is met`
      AND `the condition in paragraph (g) is met`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Nothing in subsection (1) prohibits the giving by a company of financial assistance ... if (a) ... (g)" -- a carve-out named for a permission whose "if" gate failed {F-A7}

§ `Section 76(9BA): the route where the assistance does not materially prejudice`

-- (9BA)(a): giving the assistance does not materially prejudice (i) the interests of the company or its shareholders; or (ii) the company's ability to pay its creditors.
-- Read as: it prejudices neither (fork F-A10); the other reading is that not prejudicing either one suffices.
-- src:7740 | (9BA) Nothing in subsection (1) prohibits the giving by a company
-- src:7741 | of financial assistance for the purpose of, or in connection with, an
-- src:7742 | acquisition or proposed acquisition by a person of shares or units of
-- src:7743 | shares in the company or in a holding company or ultimate holding
-- src:7744 | company (as the case may be) of the company if —
-- src:7746 | (a) giving the assistance does not materially prejudice —
-- src:7748 | (i) the interests of the company or its shareholders; or
-- src:7750 | (ii) the company’s ability to pay its creditors;
@ref s 76(9BA)(a) (src:7740-7750)
GIVEN `giving the assistance materially prejudices the interests of the company or its shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `giving the assistance materially prejudices the company's ability to pay its creditors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(9BA)(a) giving the assistance does not materially prejudice the company, its shareholders or its creditors` MEANS
    IF (NOT `giving the assistance materially prejudices the interests of the company or its shareholders`) AND (NOT `giving the assistance materially prejudices the company's ability to pay its creditors`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if (a) giving the assistance does not materially prejudice (i) the interests of the company or its shareholders; or (ii) the company's ability to pay its creditors" -- a condition introduced by "if", unmet (fork F-A10)

-- (9BA)(b): the board of directors passes a resolution that (i) the company should give the assistance; and (ii) the terms and conditions under which the assistance is proposed to be given
-- are fair and reasonable to the company.
-- src:7752 | (b) the board of directors of the company passes a resolution
-- src:7753 | that —
-- src:7755 | (i) the company should give the assistance; and
-- src:7757 | (ii) the terms and conditions under which the assistance
-- src:7758 | is proposed to be given are fair and reasonable to the
-- src:7759 | company;
@ref s 76(9BA)(b) (src:7752-7759)
