      `the resolution says the company should give the assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution says the terms and conditions under which the assistance is proposed to be given are fair and reasonable to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(9BA)(b) the board has passed the resolution the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF    `the board of directors of the company has passed a resolution`
      AND `the resolution says the company should give the assistance`
      AND `the resolution says the terms and conditions under which the assistance is proposed to be given are fair and reasonable to the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if ... (b) the board of directors of the company passes a resolution that (i) the company should give the assistance; and (ii) the terms and conditions ... are fair and reasonable to the company" -- a condition introduced by "if", unmet

