§ `Section 76(9C) and (9CA): what ends the routes before the assistance is given`

-- (9C): a company must not give financial assistance under (9A) or (9B) if, before the assistance is given, (a) any of the directors who voted in favour of the resolution (i) ceases
-- to be satisfied that the giving is in the best interests of the company; or (ii) ceases to be satisfied that the terms are fair and reasonable to the company; or (b) any of the directors
-- no longer has reasonable grounds for any of the opinions expressed in the solvency statement.
-- src:7769 | (9C) A company must not give financial assistance under
-- src:7770 | subsection (9A) or (9B) if, before the assistance is given —
-- src:7772 | (a) any of the directors who voted in favour of the resolution
-- src:7773 | under subsection (9A)(c) or (9B)(a), respectively —
-- src:7775 | (i) ceases to be satisfied that the giving of the assistance
-- src:7776 | is in the best interests of the company; or
-- src:7778 | (ii) ceases to be satisfied that the terms and conditions
-- src:7779 | under which the assistance is proposed are fair and
-- src:7780 | reasonable to the company; or
-- src:7782 | (b) any of the directors no longer has reasonable grounds for
-- src:7783 | any of the opinions expressed in the solvency statement.
@ref s 76(9C) (src:7769-7783)
GIVEN `the assistance is to be given under subsection (9A) or (9B)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a director who voted in favour of the resolution has ceased to be satisfied that the giving of the assistance is in the best interests of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a director who voted in favour of the resolution has ceased to be satisfied that the terms and conditions under which the assistance is proposed are fair and reasonable to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a director no longer has reasonable grounds for an opinion expressed in the solvency statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(9C) the company is barred from giving the assistance under subsection (9A) or (9B)` MEANS
    IF NOT `the assistance is to be given under subsection (9A) or (9B)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar speaks of financial assistance "under subsection (9A) or (9B)" and says nothing of assistance given another way (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))
    ELSE (IF    `a director who voted in favour of the resolution has ceased to be satisfied that the giving of the assistance is in the best interests of the company`
             OR `a director who voted in favour of the resolution has ceased to be satisfied that the terms and conditions under which the assistance is proposed are fair and reasonable to the company`
             OR `a director no longer has reasonable grounds for an opinion expressed in the solvency statement`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must not give financial assistance under subsection (9A) or (9B) if, before the assistance is given" -- a bar whose "if" gate failed: the provision's own question (marginal reading (a); fork F-A11)

-- src:7769 | (9C) A company must not give financial assistance under
-- src:7770 | subsection (9A) or (9B) if, before the assistance is given —
-- src:7772 | (a) any of the directors who voted in favour of the resolution
-- src:7773 | under subsection (9A)(c) or (9B)(a), respectively —
-- src:7775 | (i) ceases to be satisfied that the giving of the assistance
-- src:7776 | is in the best interests of the company; or
-- src:7778 | (ii) ceases to be satisfied that the terms and conditions
-- src:7779 | under which the assistance is proposed are fair and
-- src:7780 | reasonable to the company; or
-- src:7782 | (b) any of the directors no longer has reasonable grounds for
-- src:7783 | any of the opinions expressed in the solvency statement.
@ref s 76(9C) (src:7769-7783)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 76 act`
`s 76(9C) a company must not give the assistance under subsection (9A) or (9B) once a director has ceased to be satisfied` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    SHANT `s 76(9C) give financial assistance under subsection (9A) or (9B) after a director has ceased to be satisfied or no longer has reasonable grounds`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company gave financial assistance under subsection (9A) or (9B) after a director who voted for the resolution ceased to be satisfied, or a director no longer had reasonable grounds for an opinion in the solvency statement"

-- (9CA): a company must not give financial assistance under (9BA) if, before the assistance is given, any of the directors who voted in favour of the resolution under (9BA)(b) ceases to be
