    IF NOT `the assistance is to be given under subsection (9BA)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar speaks of financial assistance "under subsection (9BA)" and says nothing of assistance given another way (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))
    ELSE (IF `a director who voted in favour of the resolution has ceased to be satisfied that the terms and conditions under which the assistance is proposed are fair and reasonable to the company`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must not give financial assistance under subsection (9BA) if, before the assistance is given, any of the directors who voted in favour ... ceases to be satisfied" -- a bar whose "if" gate failed: the provision's own question (marginal reading (a); fork F-A11)

